------- FILE main.asm
------- FILE drums.asm LEVEL 2 PASS 3
      0  4ae6					      include	"drums.asm"
      1  4ae6							; Fat Chip 64 - drums on the MidiNES
      2  4ae6							;
      3  4ae6							; Two sources, one kit:
      4  4ae6							;   the keytar's rhythm   MIDI in channel 16 (Yamaha SHS-10: 45 kick, 48 tom,
      5  4ae6							;			   52 snare, 57 hat, 62 cymbal; velocity 127 = accent,
      6  4ae6							;			   64 = hit, 56 = ghost)
      7  4ae6							;   the beat demos	   G picks one of six Beat Lab beats (and its kit),
      8  4ae6							;			   RETURN starts / stops it, at its own tempo (B taps
      9  4ae6							;			   a new one)
     10  4ae6							; Kick, snare, toms and percussion are samples on the MidiNES's sample
     11  4ae6							; channel (one at a time: a hit within DRUM_WINDOW ms of a more important one
     12  4ae6							; is dropped; kick > snare > tom > perc). Hats and cymbals are NES noise:
     13  4ae6							; a note-on, then a note-off after the sound's length, the level set with
     14  4ae6							; CC7; closed hats vary their note and level a little on each hit (the Beat
